              "step": "On the candidate-demand incidence graph, branch on candidates covering at least n^δ remaining demands. The number of inclusions per branch is at most n/n^δ, and the remaining incidences give a CNF of length O(n^(1+δ) polylog n). Choosing δ small enough transfers any fixed power saving for SAT."
